{"user": "At the very end I got skipped on a turn (no legal move) right before White grabbed b6. Was that skip unavoidable, or did I mess up earlier and give White that last square for free?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T20:28:40.373369+00:00", "assistant": "The **skip itself was unavoidable** once you reached that position: in Othello, if Black has **no legal move**, Black must pass; then White moves if White has any legal move.\n\nSo White didn\u2019t \u201csteal\u201d b6 illegally \u2014 your pass was forced.\n\nBut strategically, a forced pass usually means the earlier sequence gave White **mobility control**: they left you with no legal move while keeping **b6** for themselves. So the mistake, if any, happened **earlier**, not on the skipped turn.\n\nFinal count from the board: **Black 29, White 35**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T20:28:40.373369+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T20:28:45.373369+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1, "Common Ground Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Negative Feedback": 2, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Negative Feedback": 0.6666666666666666, "Local Justification": 0